{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nThe plan-review Pass-3 veto `veto:cited-reference-inaccurate` (`src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py`, `pass3_decide`) drops a finding whenever the Pass-2 verifier answers `cited_reference_accurate == \"no\"`. That rule is deterministic and compares no locations; the defect is in the question the verifier is asked. Neither plan-review verifier prompt says whose citation the question is about. When a finding's claim is that the PLAN's citation is wrong, the verifier checks the plan's citation, finds it wrong, and answers `no`, so the gate drops the finding exactly when it is correct.\n\nEvidence: all 5 drops reported on this ticket carry `cited_reference_accurate: \"no\"` with `evidence_entails_finding: \"yes\"` in their saved `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecars. Measured verifier behaviour (3 samples per arm) is in the ticket comments.\n\n## Prior intent\n\nEpic messy-moose-jig and `evals/plan-review-gate/harnesses/three_pass.py` aim Pass-2 skepticism at the FINDING and scope the veto to \"a code citation present\" in the finding's evidence. Nothing documents vetoing a finding because the plan's citation is wrong. The fix restores that purpose.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. In `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier_agentic.md`, replace the paragraph beginning \"cited_reference_accurate is yes|no|insufficient|na — for a finding that cites a specific code reference, VERIFY the citation with read_file/search_files\" with one that keeps the read_file/search_files instruction and adds: the question tests the finding's OWN evidence references; `no` means the finding's evidence does not show what the finding says and vetoes it; a reference the PLAN makes is not the finding's citation, so a finding that correctly reports a wrong plan citation is `yes`, never `no`; a corrected location the finding offers is judged as its own evidence.\n2. In `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier.md` (single-turn, no tools), replace the paragraph beginning \"cited_reference_accurate is yes|no|insufficient|na — answer it only when the finding cites a specific code reference, else na\" with the same scoping, without the tool instruction.\n3. In `docs/plan-review-gate.md`, change the decision-rule sentence \"the only veto is `cited_reference_accurate == \"no\"` (fires only when a finding cites a specific code reference)\" to say it fires when the finding's OWN cited reference is refuted, not when the finding reports a wrong plan citation.\n4. Add `tests/external/test_cited_reference_veto_scope_live.py`, parametrized over both verifier prompts. Fixture: a plan with two wrong citations (nonexistent `tests/unit/test_init_ensures_seam.py`; `AGENTS.md:215`), two correct findings reporting them, and a control finding whose own evidence cites a wrong location. Per variant, by majority of 3 runs (measured margin: 3/3 on the fixed prompts for both variants; 0/3 agentic and 1/3 single-turn on the unfixed prompts, recorded in a comment): no plan-citation finding is vetoed or unverified. For the agentic variant the control must also be vetoed (the single-turn verifier has no tools to read the control's lines). The kernel enforces verifier prompt rules behaviorally rather than by prompt-text greps (`review_kernel/verify.py`), so this test lives in the external live tier.\n\nNo change to `pass3_decide`, Pass-2 verifier variance handling, or cross-criterion grouping.\n\n`code-review-verify.md` has the same unscoped wording and feeds the same veto, but it is a separate gate whose verdicts live with the review-bot, and no code-review drop of this shape has been measured. Changing it without that measurement would alter every Gerrit `LLM-Review` vote on untested behaviour. It is filed as asthmatic-bemused-wyvern (linked `discovered_from`), which measures code-review drops first and applies the same scoping if any are found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A ticket comment records the veto's decision rule from `pass3_decide` and the sidecar evidence that prompt wording, not a location comparison, made it fire.\n- [ ] The agentic verifier prompt carries the scoped `cited_reference_accurate` rule.\n- [ ] The single-turn verifier prompt carries the scoped `cited_reference_accurate` rule.\n- [ ] `docs/plan-review-gate.md`'s decision-rule sentence states the veto fires on the finding's own refuted citation.\n- [ ] The live test passes for both variants on the fixed prompts.\n- [ ] The live test fails for both variants on the unfixed prompts (measured, recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] One `review-plan` on a throwaway ticket carrying the case-2 mis-citation (`CHANGELOG.md:371` for the v0.12.0 `REBAR_LLM_MODEL` removal) is run after the fix, and its result is recorded in a comment with the sidecar reason for the citation finding.\n- [ ] A comment maps all 5 recorded cases to the fix: cases 1, 2 and 4 are reproduced in the fixture or throwaway review; cases 3 and 5 share their shape.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` passes.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit/test_criteria_vocabulary_reviewers.py tests/unit/test_review_kernel.py tests/unit/test_plan_review.py` passes.\n\n## Testing\n`pytest tests/unit/test_criteria_vocabulary_reviewers.py tests/unit/test_review_kernel.py tests/unit/test_plan_review.py`; `REBAR_RUN_EXTERNAL=1 pytest -m external tests/external/test_cited_reference_veto_scope_live.py` (needs provider credentials)."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793505072102235001,"uuid":"d7667f3a-f94a-43ee-8840-418221cbb6c1"}